A||||15||loafer87gt||98 Ram Air Trans Am gets slaughtered by ricer||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||08-15-2000||12:57 PM||||I was cruising with my buddiy the other night in his 98 ram air Trans Am. First off, let me say, this is one hell of a fast car! Anyways, we were going over one of the main bridges in town and we heard this LOUD scream coming up behind us, and a early 90's Talon flew past us. We both kinda laughed, and at the lights at the next section we chatted with the guy behind the wheel. By the sounds of things, he was some Australian bloke. I jokingly told him thats a pretty wild exhaust system on his car. He informed me that it wasn't the muffler, but the wastegate. My buddy asked him if he was up for a race, and the guy told him that he was way out of his league. He said his runs 117 through the quarter mile. This really pissed off my buddy, and when the lights went green, we both took off and by the time we were doing around a 100 MPH he was about 3 or 4 cars ahead of us. Christ, i have seen those Talons hopped up in Sport COmpact Car magazine before, but never before in real life. Insanely fast! ||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||08-15-2000||11:04 PM||||Not trying to be rude, but......bullsh1t. I dont believe that for one second.||||reg||1
Z||000002||olympic||08-15-2000||11:53 PM||||   I believe it!!  I hang a <A HREF="http://www.ls1.com" TARGET=_blank>www.ls1.com</A>  once in a while and occasionally someone will admit to getting beat by a Talon.  These cars arn't too quick stock but in the hands of the right person they can really scream(read: lots of boost).  Some of them are also all wheel drive so they have a big traction advantage.   Heres a quote from a Talon drivers sig:  "I've got your replacement for displacement right here!"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||08-16-2000||02:36 AM||||Believe it man...  A highly tweaked turbo DSM can be an animal.||||reg||1
Z||000004||loafer87gt||08-16-2000||04:01 AM||||I did some checking around an it isn't uncommon to see a modded Talon running 9's in the 1/4. I know damn well by the sound of this guys car that he definetly had something going on under the hood that wasn't stock. Here is a page with some numbers and links to some of the performance upgrades for the turbos talons. With a bigger intercooler, and the engine built up, they can sqeeze over 650 HP to the wheels from this powerplant. Check out the following links:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.heckconsulting.com/dsm/drag.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.heckconsulting.com/dsm/drag.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.buschurracing.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.buschurracing.com/</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||BellaFiero||08-17-2000||03:17 PM||||My best friend's father owns the WS6 Ram Air... sorry, folks, but I've seen the power in the car. Now, I know that there has to be a Talon somewhere that can beat it, but I highly doubt it's street legal... or that it costs less than a Trans Am to supe it up to that point... I mean, heck, you give me a million dollars, I'll bet I could make a Ford Aerostar eat the track alive, but no way would I be able to put the plates on her and drive it home after the pass. Did the guy have a nitrous hook up? and did his engine obtain orbit at some point during the race? <P>------------------<BR>"No, no... you can't put that there, it'll be in the way of the Johnson Rod!"  ||||reg||4
Z||000006||fiero56||08-17-2000||03:31 PM||||I believe it. I've seen some AWD Talons pull some amazing shots out of stop lights. That, and those T/As and Z28 pigs are too big for their own good. They are quick, but I have never been really impressed with them.||||reg||1
Z||000007||whamel||08-17-2000||03:40 PM||||What's the RA TA push in '98 - is it like 305hp and 325 torque?  I can't remember off the top of my head right now.  I think the Talon AWD TSI runs about 210/214 out of the box.  Not too far apart really...The weight is about the same (within a couple hundred pounds to), right?<BR>I have been building up an Acura Integra lately (just to sell it - I'll probably never even drive it) and there are guys out there that will drop $10,000 on modifications to a Honda Civic!  I guess you have to just have a fondness for the body style - since for the $10k in mods and the over $12k price of the car .. you could get into something pretty nice.  I don't understand it, but it is sure profitable!||||reg||1
Z||000008||olympic||08-17-2000||03:47 PM||||An M6 LS1 T/A or Camaro will put out ~310-315 hp at the wheels bone stock.  It's not hard to believe that a Mitsubishi 4 cylinder running say 25 psi could put out near that number at high rpm.  And with a lighter car like the Talon, its quite possible it could beat the TA.  Especially if we are comparing a 5 speed AWD Talon to a RWD automatic TA with 2.73 rear gears, for example.<P>   A while back I posted a link to a Dodge minivan with a 2.2l turbo that ran low 13's with minimal internal engine mods.  And there are plenty of SVO Mustangs with 2.3l turbos running 12's and 13's.<P>  Remember, 15 psi boost is equivalent to doubling the displacement of the engine.  And  some of these 4 bangers can take up to 30 psi.  Of course this will shorten the engines life but thaths the price you have to pay to go fast with a 4 cylinder car.||||reg||1
Z||000009||whamel||08-17-2000||03:56 PM||||Quite true - with very little modification my 2.2L Dodge went from 220hp up to 290hp.  Simple stuff like adding a BOV and cleaning up some of the plumbing that Dodge screwed up when they installed it helped a bunch.  Adding a better air intake and a good exhaust system helped too.  I probably could have done more with it, but that Turbo III engine was wound pretty tight as it is and the tremendous replacement cost was a bummer.  I can only imagine what somebody could do with a similiar setup, but a more stable head/block combo than I had, and I imagine the Talon has to be about the closest car I can think of to that one.||||reg||1
Z||000010||My7Fieros||08-18-2000||12:09 AM||||Jeez......  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cooter||08-18-2000||12:41 AM||||My cousin has an Eagle AWD turbo, completly stock and it is really scary fast! On the bright side (for us-not him), he has replaced the clutch 3 times and the turbo twice and he is pretty conservative behind the wheel. Those highly boosted turbo cars are impressive, but I wonder what you could do with a v8 and have that kind of mod's on it. What about an LS-1 turbo or S/C in the Fiero? I wonder how the amount spent would compare to that spent to modify the Talons/Eclipses.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Dan86gt3.8||08-18-2000||03:17 AM||||Well this place: <A HREF="http://www.turbotechnologyinc.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.turbotechnologyinc.com/</A>   just got through with thier SINGLE turbo that runs ethier 6.5 or 7.5 lbs of boost and it is pushing 491 RWHP.  I heard about it on ls1.com .  I think the kit was around $7,000<BR>His only other mod was a mufflex 4"exhaust.  It was also on a all stock motor.  He boastd that on the way home from getting it tuned he was on the highway with his bud that drove a 11.80 second viper and that he would let the viper downshift and take off then he would floor it and just blow past him.  I don't know if there is any truth to that but hey if he has 491 rwhp it could defenitely be true especailly in the top end like that.<BR>Meanwhile there are tons of idiot ls1 owners that are waiting for a twin turbo system that is still trying to be worked out. <P> And about that talon it could have ben hopped up to any ungodly amount of boost.  And once again the damned ls1's are not unbeatable (yes they are very fast) but NOT unbeatable.  There are 1,000's of hooped up mustangs around that can smoke them.  Its just the typical ls1 owners want you to believe that thier engine is the fastest thing on the streets.... period ||||reg||1
Z||000013||olympic||08-18-2000||03:24 AM||||A company called INCON is developing a twin turbo kit for the LS1.  Unfortunately, because the LS1 is a high compression motor(10:1) the boost is limited to 6-8 psi.  It will still produce over 450 hp though.<P>  A purpose built, low compression small block V8 with twin turbos can easily produce 800 hp.  Some turboed small block Mustangs are well over 1000 hp||||reg||1
Z||000014||olympic||08-18-2000||03:28 AM||||I think I have to learn to type faster  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000015||Dan86gt3.8||08-19-2000||11:41 AM||||ya incon is the company I was referring to.  They are making a stage one and stage 2I think stage one is going to be like 450 hp.  and stage 2 is something like 650 or 700 hp.  They actaully have the turbos physically in the prototype car right now, but can't get it to run right and are having big tuning problems.  So they still have to get all that crap worked out and get the 200 guys waiting for thier turbo kits thier turbos before they can start selling them to other guys.  But hey if I could get darn near 500 rwhp out of a single turbo right now with no wait then heck ya I would be all over it.  but just an opinion....||||reg||1
